  "notes": [
    "All hex is lowercase. Every *_hex expectation is an output; every other field is an input.",
    "Typed value encoding (fundamentals §§3-4): {\"type\":\"bytes\",\"hex\":..} raw bytes; {\"type\":\"string\",\"utf8\":..} strict UTF-8 bytes; {\"type\":\"uint32\"|\"uint64\"|\"enum\",\"value\":..} 4/8/4-byte big-endian; {\"type\":\"bool\",\"value\":..} 0x00/0x01; {\"type\":\"repeat\",\"hex\":..,\"count\":..} the unit repeated count times; {\"type\":\"frame\",\"fields\":[..]} a nested FRAME_V1 with no domain prefix.",
    "H_V1: frame = ascii(\"TRUEOPEN_FRAME_V1\") || u32_be(len(domain)) || domain || u64_be(len(payload)) || payload; hash = SHA256(frame).",
    "H_FIELDS_V1: frame = u64_be(len(domain)) || domain || for each field u64_be(len(field)) || field; hash = SHA256(frame).",
    "Composite primitives (fundamentals §§4.4/10.3) publish raw value layouts, not hashes: REPEATED_V1 frames count then elements; OPTIONAL_V1 is absent 00 or present 01 || FRAME_V1(value); ONEOF_V1 is u32_be(field_number) || FRAME_V1(selected payload fields).",
    "MERKLE_ROOT_V1: leaf = SHA256(leaf_prefix || u32_be(len(domain)) || domain || leaf_hash); node = SHA256(node_prefix || u32_be(len(domain)) || domain || left || right); empty root = SHA256(empty_prefix || u32_be(len(domain)) || domain). A trailing odd node is promoted unchanged: no duplication, no zero padding, no power-of-two levels. The empty root is never the 32-byte zero value.",
    "frame_hex is only carried when include_frame is true; oversized payloads publish the hash only.",
    "signature_digest = SHA256(raw 64-byte R||S), never SHA256 of the hex text (§1.3 rule 5).",
    "signature_v1 signs a MESSAGE: the signer hashes it once, so a verifier that hashes the message once accepts. signature_direct_digest_v1 signs an already-derived 32-byte SIGN_DIGEST as-is, which is the only form fundamentals §10.5 and task_specification §10.3 allow for a digest the contract names. The two are separate sections because their verifiers are not interchangeable: digest_hex = SHA256(digest_message) is signed directly, and rehashed_digest_hex = SHA256(digest_hex) is the value a one-extra-hash verifier would check against. That verification must FAIL, so an implementation that reaches for a generic \"verify this message\" call cannot pass this vector.",
    "Signature rejects are named mutations of a valid vector: uppercase_hex, prepend_space, append_space, append_zero_byte (65 bytes), prepend_recovery_byte (Cosmos 65-byte form and, by the same length rule, DER), drop_last_byte, drop_last_hex_char (odd hex length), replace_last_hex_char_with_z (non-hex), negate_s (s -\u003e N-s, high-S), zero_r, zero_s.",
    "Regenerate with TRUEOPEN_REGEN_FIXTURES=1; the run rewrites expectations and then fails on purpose so the diff must be reviewed against the frozen contract."
  ],
